WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:04.910
Kevin Sorbo's time in the spotlight has diminished
since his Hercules days, but if you think

00:00:04.910 --> 00:00:07.680
you've seen him around lately, you might just
be right.

00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:09.600
Keep watching to see what he's been up to!

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:14.740
In 2012, Sorbo published a book containing
some shocking revelations.

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:21.220
In the later seasons of Hercules: The Legendary
Journeys, which aired from 1994 to 1999, viewers

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:25.600
started to notice a shift away from the title
character and onto the shoulders of other

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:26.100
stars.

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:30.960
No one knew why there was a sudden flood of
guest stars, and it wasn't until Sorbo published

00:00:30.970 --> 00:00:36.540
his book that fans learned the truth: in 1997,
he suffered three strokes as the result of

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:37.040
an aneurysm.

00:00:37.860 --> 00:00:42.700
True Strength: My Journey from Hercules to
Mere Mortal How Nearly Dying Saved My Life

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:45.060
is the story of just what happened to Sorbo.

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:48.899
He was in the middle of a promotional tour
for Kull the Conqueror when he started to

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:53.340
feel some odd sensations in his left hand
and arm, but doctors brushed it off.

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:57.140
The pain worsened during a workout, and he
went to his chiropractor.

00:00:57.560 --> 00:01:01.100
After driving home, he started suffering all
the symptoms of a stroke.

00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:05.860
It was then that doctors discovered and removed
the aneurysm that was blocking blood flow

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:06.480
to his arm.

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:12.040
After returning to the Hercules set, Sorbo
endured aftereffects like fatigue, depression,

00:01:12.040 --> 00:01:13.140
and anxiety attacks.

00:01:13.550 --> 00:01:18.660
He still suffers from nerve damage, residual
pain, the occasional migraine, and a ten percent

00:01:18.670 --> 00:01:23.470
loss of vision, and he says that the experience
made him realize what was truly important

00:01:23.470 --> 00:01:25.100
to him: his wife and his faith.

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:29.100
It also made him want to share his story in
the hopes of helping others through similar

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:29.780
experiences.

00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:32.960
"We are survivors and we should never, ever
give up."

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:39.680
In 2014, fantasy fans got to see Sorbo don
his medieval gear once again with the release

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:44.150
of Mythica: A Quest for Heroes, his second
collaboration with the production company

00:01:44.150 --> 00:01:44.800
Arrowstorm.

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:49.670
When he was approached to read the script,
he was absolutely and unconditionally on board,

00:01:49.670 --> 00:01:53.200
even though he was playing the wizard rather
than the warrior this time around.

00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:59.670
More Mythica movies followed, with The Darkspore
and The Necromancer arriving in 2015, and

00:01:59.670 --> 00:02:03.380
then The Iron Crown and The Godslayer in 2016.

00:02:03.660 --> 00:02:08.840
When Sorbo spoke with Geek Dad in 2015, he
acknowledged that while his role as the heroine's

00:02:08.840 --> 00:02:12.940
mentor was limited in the initial film, he
was going to play a bigger part as the story

00:02:12.940 --> 00:02:13.440
went on.

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:17.380
When he was asked why fantasy had become his
go-to genre, he admitted,

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:18.640
"Love that world.

00:02:18.820 --> 00:02:20.140
No rules in the fantasy world.

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:22.740
Writers can do what they want and make it
come to life.

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:24.460
Just fun to be a part of the fantasy."

00:02:25.160 --> 00:02:30.120
Sorbo became famous for his portrayal of a
legendary character, and in 2017 news broke

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:32.900
that he'd soon be associated with another
famous franchise.

00:02:33.160 --> 00:02:36.640
When it was first revealed that he would be
playing a recurring character on The CW's

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:40.440
Supergirl, he was simply described as one
of the show's many bad guys.

00:02:40.880 --> 00:02:45.120
The mystery surrounding just who he was going
to portray built for more than a month.

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:49.540
That's practically forever in internet time,
but finally the studio eventually confirmed

00:02:49.540 --> 00:02:53.540
that he'd be stepping into the boots of Mon-El's
father, Lar Gand.

00:02:53.980 --> 00:02:58.500
Sorbo ended up appearing in a three-episode
arc, with former Lois Lane Teri Hatcher playing

00:02:58.500 --> 00:02:59.040
his wife.

00:02:59.340 --> 00:03:02.560
In an interview with Entertainment Tonight,
he revealed that if things had gone a little

00:03:02.569 --> 00:03:07.790
differently back in 1993, he would've ended
up playing Superman opposite Hatcher in Lois

00:03:07.790 --> 00:03:09.460
&amp; Clark: The New Adventures of Superman.

00:03:09.820 --> 00:03:12.860
But, alas, that part ultimately went to Dean
Cain instead.

00:03:14.580 --> 00:03:19.040
Sorbo is a devout Christian, and recent years
have seen him frequently turning his attention

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:20.330
to faith-based films.

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:25.740
In 2014's God's Not Dead, he stars as an atheist
professor who challenges his students' views

00:03:25.740 --> 00:03:27.040
on the existence of God.

00:03:27.260 --> 00:03:27.760
"God.

00:03:28.220 --> 00:03:28.720
Is.

00:03:29.080 --> 00:03:29.580
Dead."

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:35.080
In 2014, he was also in Revelation Road: The
Black Rider, a tale about what's left after

00:03:35.080 --> 00:03:39.520
the Rapture, and Let the Lion Roar, in which
he played Reformation leader John Calvin.

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:44.160
He even played Joseph in 2016's Joseph and
Mary, a retelling of one of the Bible's most

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:45.200
well-known stories.

00:03:45.660 --> 00:03:50.520
In a 2016 interview with Gospel Herald, he
spoke about why he thought bringing faith-based

00:03:50.520 --> 00:03:52.140
films to the big screen was important:

00:03:52.380 --> 00:03:56.440
"I think that most people would agree that
faith-based movies back in the '70s, '80s,

00:03:56.440 --> 00:04:00.900
and even the '90s were very cheesy, poorly
written, and poorly acted.

00:04:01.060 --> 00:04:04.320
A lot of people were turned off by them, because
they were also too preachy.

00:04:04.660 --> 00:04:07.960
We live in a world where people don't want
to be told what to believe in and what not

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:08.560
to believe in.

00:04:08.820 --> 00:04:10.920
You have to walk a fine line to hold an audience."

00:04:11.120 --> 00:04:16.099
Sorbo shows no sign of slowing down, even
teaming up with Fox News' Sean Hannity for

00:04:16.100 --> 00:04:19.760
Let There be Light, which is about an atheist
who has a near-death experience.

00:04:20.580 --> 00:04:26.000
Since 1997, Sorbo has been involved with almost
every aspect of a charity called "A World

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:26.820
Fit For Kids!"

00:04:27.340 --> 00:04:31.530
As a celebrity spokesperson, he's spoken out
about things like the nationwide drop-out

00:04:31.530 --> 00:04:36.280
rate for schools and childhood obesity, pushing
to get A World Fit For Kids! to go outside

00:04:36.280 --> 00:04:38.360
of California and into other parts of the
country.

00:04:38.620 --> 00:04:42.260
At its heart, the charity is an after-school
program that touches on everything from physical

00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:46.660
fitness, to training teens to become mentors
for younger children, to preparing kids for

00:04:46.660 --> 00:04:49.640
what they're going to be confronted with once
they reach the working world.

00:04:50.030 --> 00:04:54.480
"All kids deserve that kind of encouragement,
but the reality is, most don't get it.

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:57.700
That's why I'm involved with A World Fit for
Kids."

00:04:57.870 --> 00:05:01.960
Sorbo has headed up fundraisers and participated
in public service announcements about issues

00:05:01.960 --> 00:05:05.480
like providing workplace mentors to students
interested in pursuing their dreams.

00:05:05.480 --> 00:05:10.280
In 2005, he took on another charity role as
the spokesperson for the Afterschool Alliance,

00:05:10.420 --> 00:05:14.880
an organization dedicated to providing safe
and educational programs for students.

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:19.340
So even if you haven't seen much of Sorbo's
recent film and TV appearances, he's still

00:05:19.340 --> 00:05:22.440
been working steadily in whatever capacity
he's passionate about.

